The '''Two Centuries War''' was a series of conflicts in Illypnia that began in 1337 after the [[Great Catholic Schism]]. It was fought between the Petran Catholic states and the Zamarran Catholic states and became one of the most important conflicts of the Middle Ages in Illypnia. Later historical writing often associated the war with both the height of chivalric warfare and its subsequent decline.

== Background ==

The war emerged from the schism that divided Catholic authority between the papal states, centred on [[Volisania]], and the Zamarran court at [[Zamarra]] on [[Lake Zamarra]]. The underlying dispute involved church taxation, papal jurisdiction, indulgences, purgatory, and the authority of the Curia. Political and economic tensions in southern Illypnia also shaped the conflict, especially where trade routes and revenue streams had weakened.

== Main theatres ==

The earliest and most sustained fighting took place in the valleys of the [[Rio Grande]] and [[Rio Verde]], especially in the border zone between [[Sarta]] and [[Kingdom of Kastruneto|Kastruneto]]. Control of river corridors, valley fortresses, and mountain passes mattered as much as control of towns. Campaigns in this region were closely tied to the shifting frontiers of the two rival ecclesiastical coalitions.

Other campaigns took place across western Kastruneto and along the borders of its allies and opponents. The conflict was not a single continuous campaign but a long series of wars, truces, raids, and frontier offensives that recurred over generations.

== Chivalry and warfare ==

The Two Centuries War is often described by later historians as a high point of chivalric warfare. Armoured knights, noble retinues, ransoms, heraldry, and siege warfare remained central features of the conflict in its earlier phases. Over time, however, changing tactics, longer campaigns, and the increasing importance of revenue, logistics, and fortified terrain reduced the dominance of traditional chivalric combat.

== Alliances ==

The Zamarran coalition included [[Kingdom of Kastruneto|Kastruneto]], [[Kingdom of Breisland|Breisland]], and [[Kingdom of Nabia|Nabia]]. The papal coalition included [[Volisania]], [[Sarta]], and [[Kingdom of Jacan|Jacan]]. These alignments reflected both religious allegiance and wider political and commercial interests.

== Legacy ==

The war left a lasting mark on Illypnian politics. It reshaped church authority, hardened regional rivalries, and influenced later ideas about nobility, warfare, and kingship. In Sarta and Kastruneto, the river-valley campaigns remained central to historical memory long after the conflict itself had become a matter of dynastic and ecclesiastical history.

